// EXPECT: [E082]
// ...and the row does NOT excuse a measure the programmer WROTE. `effects diverge` waives the
// obligation the compiler would have raised on its own, but `decreasing n` is a claim, and a claim
// the compiler does not check reads as verified (D-44). Here `n` does not shrink, so the written
// measure fails and the program is refused despite the row.
//
// This is the same rule the loop path already applied (`f->may_diverge && !b->has_measure`), now
// applied to recursion — which is what makes the two sources one mechanism.
func spin(n i32) i32 effects diverge decreasing n {
    if n == 0 { return 0 }
    return spin(n)
}
func main() i32 effects diverge { return spin(1) }
